  "Question": "There are 5 points in a plane, with no three on the same line. If a line is drawn through each pair of points, how many lines can be drawn?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "10",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Since no three points are collinear, each pair determines a distinct line. Choose the first point in \\(5\\) ways and the second from the remaining \\(4\\), giving \\(5\\times4\\) ordered choices. Every pair is counted twice, once in each order, so dividing by \\(2\\) counts each pair once. There are \\(5\\times4\\div2=10\\) lines in total.",
